{
  "test_name": "memory_tools_001",
  "test_file": "data/benchmark/tests/memory_tools/memory_tools_001.json",
  "description": "Memory tools test case 1. Tests that agents can retrieve information from memory and inbox emails to perform complex email tasks. Session 1: 5 memory setup queries. Session 2: 5 emails inserted into inbox. Session 3: 5 reply/forward/send email queries requiring both memory and email information.",
  "session_id": "bench_b51ce4ca",
  "timestamp": "2025-11-03T12:00:00",
  "overall_success": false,
  "steps": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "user_message": "Note that I studied for 3 hours on Monday, 4 hours on Tuesday, and 2.5 hours on Wednesday for my exam.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I studied for 3 hours on Monday, 4 hours on Tuesday, and 2.5 hours on Wednesday for my exam",
      "agent_response": "Got it — you studied 3 hours (Mon), 4 hours (Tue), and 2.5 hours (Wed). Total = 9.5 hours.\n\nWhat would you like me to do with this note? Options:\n- Send an email reporting these study hours to someone (tell me the recipient and any extra message).\n- Save it as a draft in your drafts folder.\n- Log it to yourself (I can send an email to your own address with this summary).\n- Just keep this as a note (no email action).\n\nIf you want to send or draft, here are quick templates — tell me which one to use and the recipient:\n\n1) To a professor / instructor\nSubject: Study hours for exam prep (Mon–Wed)\nBody:\nHi [Professor Name],\nI wanted to let you know I studied 3 hours on Monday, 4 hours on Tuesday, and 2.5 hours on Wednesday — total 9.5 hours — while preparing for the exam. Please let me know if you have any suggestions or resources I should focus on.\nThanks,\n[Your Name]\n\n2) To a study partner\nSubject: Study update (Mon–Wed)\nBody:\nHey [Name],\nQuick update — I studied 3h on Mon, 4h on Tue, and 2.5h on Wed (9.5h total). How are you doing with prep?\nCheers,\n[Your Name]\n\n3) Personal log (send to yourself or save as draft)\nSubject: Study log — Mon–Wed\nBody:\nStudy log:\n- Monday: 3.0 hours\n- Tuesday: 4.0 hours\n- Wednesday: 2.5 hours\nTotal: 9.5 hours\n\nTell me which action and template (and the recipient/address) and I’ll take care of it.",
      "duration_s": 14.351,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "user_message": "I want you to remember that I took my blood pressure medication at 8 AM and 8 PM today, and my readings were 120/80 in the morning and 118/78 in the evening.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I took my blood pressure medication at 8 AM and 8 PM today, and my readings were 120/80 in the morning and 118/78 in the evening",
      "agent_response": "Got it — I’ve noted everything.\n\nSummary I’ll remember:\n- Study hours: Monday 3.0 h, Tuesday 4.0 h, Wednesday 2.5 h — Total 9.5 hours.\n- Blood pressure / medication today: took medication at 8:00 AM and 8:00 PM. Readings: 120/80 (morning), 118/78 (evening).\n\nWhat would you like me to do with this? Options:\n- Send an email now (tell me recipient and any extra message).\n- Save it as a draft (tell me recipient or say “to myself”).\n- Log it to your own email (I can send this summary to your address).\n- Just keep it as a note (no email action).\n\nIf you want an email/draft, pick a template:\nA) To your doctor:\nSubject: Blood pressure and medication update (today)\nBody: Hi [Doctor Name], I took my blood pressure medication at 8:00 AM and 8:00 PM today. Readings were 120/80 (AM) and 118/78 (PM). Also studied 3h (Mon), 4h (Tue), 2.5h (Wed) — 9.5h total. —[Your Name]\n\nB) Personal log (to yourself):\nSubject: Study & BP log — [today’s date]\nBody: Study: Mon 3.0h / Tue 4.0h / Wed 2.5h — Total 9.5h. BP meds at 8:00 AM and 8:00 PM. Readings: 120/80 (AM), 118/78 (PM).\n\nTell me which action and which template (or give a custom message/recipient) and I’ll take care of it.",
      "duration_s": 21.405,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "user_message": "Save this to memory: I had oatmeal with berries for breakfast, a chicken salad for lunch, and salmon with vegetables for dinner today.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I had oatmeal with berries for breakfast, a chicken salad for lunch, and salmon with vegetables for dinner today",
      "agent_response": "Done — I’ve saved that to your memories.\n\nStored memory:\n- Today’s meals: breakfast — oatmeal with berries; lunch — chicken salad; dinner — salmon with vegetables.\n\nWould you like me to:\n- Email or log this meal summary somewhere,\n- Add it to a diet/health report,\n- Or save any other details (calories, portion sizes, or how you felt after meals)?",
      "duration_s": 14.131,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "user_message": "Note that I drank 6 glasses of water today, which is 48 ounces total.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I drank 6 glasses of water today, which is 48 ounces total",
      "agent_response": "Saved — I've added this to your memories.\n\nStored memory:\n- Drank 6 glasses of water today (48 ounces).\n\nWould you like me to:\n- Email or log this hydration entry somewhere,\n- Add it to a daily health/diet summary,\n- Set a hydration reminder or goal,\n- Or just keep this as a note?",
      "duration_s": 15.308,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "user_message": "Note that I spent $85 on a business lunch, $45 on parking, and $120 on a train ticket for the client meeting.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I spent $85 on a business lunch, $45 on parking, and $120 on a train ticket for the client meeting",
      "agent_response": "Saved — I’ve added this to your memories.\n\nStored memory entry:\n- Expenses for client meeting: business lunch $85, parking $45, train ticket $120. Total = $250.\n\nWhat would you like me to do next?\n- Send an email/report now (tell me recipient and any extra note — I can use one of the templates below).\n- Save this as a draft (tell me recipient or say “to myself”).\n- Create a simple expense summary (CSV or text) for download.\n- Just keep it as a memory (no further action).\n\nQuick email templates you can pick from or customize:\nA) To Finance / Reimbursements\nSubject: Expense report — client meeting\nBody: Hi [Finance Name], I incurred the following expenses for the client meeting: business lunch $85, parking $45, train ticket $120. Total $250. Please let me know if you need receipts or further details. Thanks, [Your Name]\n\nB) To Manager / Approval\nSubject: Approval request — client meeting expenses\nBody: Hi [Manager Name], Requesting approval for $250 in expenses from the client meeting (lunch $85, parking $45, train $120). Receipts available on request. Thanks, [Your Name]\n\nC) Personal log (to yourself)\nSubject: Expense log — client meeting\nBody: Business lunch $85; Parking $45; Train ticket $120; Total $250.\n\nTell me which action and template (and the recipient email or any custom wording) and I’ll take care of it.",
      "duration_s": 24.899,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "step_type": "start_new_session",
